    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31088" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noctŭa</span></b> , ae, f.
		nox, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				night-owl, an owl</i>, a bird sacred to Minerva: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noctua, quod noctu canit ac vigilat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 76</span></i>
			 Müll.; Paul. ex Fest. pp. 174 and 175 ib.; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men.
				4, 2, 90</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noctuarum dimicatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 17, 19, § 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">garrula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 35, 87, § 362</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seros exercet noctua cantūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 403</span></i>
			.</div>
